note factors writes the prime factors of value into o, smallest first and with repetition, and
note returns how many it wrote.
note Check it with: sh exercise.sh exercises/prime-factors
om2
fn factors value ulong o edit ulong * to ulong
note replace this line with your solution
trap 13
end
